                        ],
                        "form": "чесучо́вых"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a6df2df4-f06f-37e1-b29a-3978357385f2",
                        "entry_id": "66a01c5b-08a0-3efd-b396-e1da2d7a01ce",
                        "glosses": [
                            "связанный, соотносящийся по значению с существительным чесуча"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f4903cad-8dd6-492f-86c9-671c0e906cd4",
                                "sense_id": "a6df2df4-f06f-37e1-b29a-3978357385f2",
                                "text": "Охотничий глаз великого комбинатора быстро распознал чесучового гражданина."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9d4d609c-626b-3a45-977d-420a790794d0",
                        "entry_id": "66a01c5b-08a0-3efd-b396-e1da2d7a01ce",
                        "glosses": [
                            "сделанный, сшитый из чесучи"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ae6480a0-c7f0-45a2-923f-d7c821f5252a",
                                "sense_id": "9d4d609c-626b-3a45-977d-420a790794d0",
                                "text": "Был он очень стар, но крепок и жилист, загорелый, с блестящей лысиной, с гладко выбритыми щеками, в ослепительно-белом чесучёвом костюме."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6bc03e27-f096-41ba-9f82-89367e99eb65",
                                "sense_id": "9d4d609c-626b-3a45-977d-420a790794d0",
                                "text": "❬…❭ одежда его намекала на принадлежность к партийной администрации, хотя он к ней никакого отношения не имел. Одет он был в чесучовый китель и в широкие галифе с сапогами. Так что, если судить по одежде, можно было сказать, что, начиная от головы и до пояса, он как бы представлял законодательную власть, а от пояса до сапог — исполнительную."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e1e403a6-f183-4ec7-8094-bb3a14125afc",
                        "source_entry_id": "66a01c5b-08a0-3efd-b396-e1da2d7a01ce",
                        "target_lang_word": "silken",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "silken",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aebfcb86-8d05-362f-b106-e5200d655bea",
                                        "entry_id": "60d60ff0-0972-3022-a732-f2b133b22472",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Made of silk."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6bc7528b-0f9b-4c91-9064-9a76352ade8d",
                                                "sense_id": "aebfcb86-8d05-362f-b106-e5200d655bea",
                                                "text": "a silken veil"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5319555b-208c-3e59-a152-716b1611bbbd",
                                        "entry_id": "60d60ff0-0972-3022-a732-f2b133b22472",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of silky, like silk, silklike, particularly",
                                            "Having a smooth, soft, or light texture."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c206218c-ecf4-4a8f-b97a-722eb329bc64",
                                                "sense_id": "5319555b-208c-3e59-a152-716b1611bbbd",
                                                "text": "Come then youth, Beauty, and Blood, all ye soft powers, / Whose silken flatteryes swell a few fond houres."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b1262a0a-b477-4811-b620-5511d8ecc5bb",
                                                "sense_id": "5319555b-208c-3e59-a152-716b1611bbbd",
                                                "text": "[L]ove is not to be bought, in any ſenſe of the vvords, its ſilken vvings are inſtantly ſhrivelled up vvhen any thing beſide a return in kind is ſought."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "210132da-2d3d-4a7c-8871-d403ee113600",
                                                "sense_id": "5319555b-208c-3e59-a152-716b1611bbbd",
                                                "text": "[…] in spite of the buzz in the next room, Edith had rolled herself up into a soft ball of muslin and ribbon, and silken curls, and gone off into a peaceful little after-dinner nap."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f348e34b-ba83-461e-90d0-e12a78e26f20",
                                                "sense_id": "5319555b-208c-3e59-a152-716b1611bbbd",
                                                "text": "He heard the silken rustle of a dressing-gown being drawn on."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0c338be9-5cd5-305d-bdd2-f6a1f4ccd49a",
                                        "entry_id": "60d60ff0-0972-3022-a732-f2b133b22472",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of silky, like silk, silklike, particularly",
                                            "Having a smooth, soft, or flowing utterance; attractive or (typically derogatory) convincing through pleasing expression."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bbaf3023-fc0c-4099-9f12-b1700e435e0d",
                                                "sense_id": "0c338be9-5cd5-305d-bdd2-f6a1f4ccd49a",
                                                "text": "Taffeta phrases, silken terms precise, / Three-piled hyperboles, spruce affectation, / Figures pedantical; these summer-flies / Have blown me full of maggot ostentation:"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "79b87b23-0965-34fe-a345-288e6aa80b64",
                                        "entry_id": "60d60ff0-0972-3022-a732-f2b133b22472",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Dressed in silk."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4400f2ee-8dff-490a-b556-daef4ee3d8f0",
                                                "sense_id": "79b87b23-0965-34fe-a345-288e6aa80b64",
                                                "text": "[S]hall a beardless boy, / A cocker’d silken wanton, brave our fields […]?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0cb0f1f1-da8e-4dba-9ae9-5d979ecfa47c",
                                                "sense_id": "79b87b23-0965-34fe-a345-288e6aa80b64",
                                                "text": "Yet though he cannot skip forth now to greet / Every fine silken painted foole we meet, / He then to him with amorous smiles allures,"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f0bb3b89-2bd6-4a7e-97d8-ce1cecc1514d",
                                                "sense_id": "79b87b23-0965-34fe-a345-288e6aa80b64",
                                                "text": "Last Saturday was three Weeks, at Two, in the Afternoon, I sent out my Servant, to watch a Couple of these Silken Strollers, and keep, if possible, within Ken of them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "32a5a4c1-8020-49fe-b7fe-d4dbf020ed57",
                                                "sense_id": "79b87b23-0965-34fe-a345-288e6aa80b64",
                                                "text": "[…] the Viceroy moved magnificently through India, resplendent with all the colour and dash of the vast Empire at his feet, with his superb bodyguard jangling scarlet beside his carriage, silken Indian princes bowing at his carpet, generals quivering at the salute and ceremonial salutes of thirty-one guns […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "silken",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "df153888-51ff-337f-9482-443104c19493",
                                        "entry_id": "55ad8d61-603f-30db-a94a-3bc848f1db9c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To render silken or silklike."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "700eb723-2026-4bb5-b79e-c108cf10e10b",
                                                "sense_id": "df153888-51ff-337f-9482-443104c19493",
                                                "text": "silkening body lotion"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "36df4f87-9799-42a8-ad2d-b0c81d87d94b",
                                                "sense_id": "df153888-51ff-337f-9482-443104c19493",
                                                "text": "Or, if your sheep are of Silurian breed,\nNightly to house them dry on fern or straw,\nSilk’ning their fleeces."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f54af02-1813-4d7d-858b-2619520430a7",
                                                "sense_id": "df153888-51ff-337f-9482-443104c19493",
                                                "text": "[…] these lights silkened her black skin:"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0281a3f0-42cd-4329-b3d3-5da1bf1d0ca4",
                        "source_entry_id": "66a01c5b-08a0-3efd-b396-e1da2d7a01ce",
                        "target_lang_word": "silk",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "silk",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "30e206b7-2dd4-3867-991d-539caacbc2d9",
                                        "entry_id": "d943f227-e916-3cc1-b723-a4ba7953b14b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A fine fiber excreted by the silkworm or other arthropod (such as a spider)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "373984c0-468d-49fe-b230-3434951f336e",
                                                "sense_id": "30e206b7-2dd4-3867-991d-539caacbc2d9",
                                                "text": "The thread made of silk was barely visible."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b4bf4c82-16af-3e4e-a151-a502ee0f89c3",
                                        "entry_id": "d943f227-e916-3cc1-b723-a4ba7953b14b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A fine, soft cloth woven from silk fibers."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8717369f-6f97-4ecf-a0aa-6d7fc88c44ca",
                                                "sense_id": "b4bf4c82-16af-3e4e-a151-a502ee0f89c3",
                                                "text": "It was flood-tide along Fifth Avenue; motor, brougham, and victoria swept by on the glittering current; pretty women glanced out from limousine and tonneau; young men of his own type, silk-hatted, frock-coated, the crooks of their walking sticks tucked up under their left arms, passed on the Park side."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "57c6bc40-926d-3ee2-a988-8d5a1ec15d49",
                                        "entry_id": "d943f227-e916-3cc1-b723-a4ba7953b14b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Anything which resembles silk, such as the filiform styles of the female flower of maize, or the seed covering of bombaxes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c876c8ac-7ee5-4390-8293-e4b5c8d9beaa",
                                                "sense_id": "57c6bc40-926d-3ee2-a988-8d5a1ec15d49",
                                                "text": "Now that she had rested and had fed from the luncheon tray Mrs. Broome had just removed, she had reverted to her normal gaiety. She looked cool in a grey tailored cotton dress with a terracotta scarf and shoes and her hair a black silk helmet."
                                            }
                                        ]
